     "type": "example",
     "title": "Worked Walkthrough: Assembling Volume MERCY001",
     "content": "Follow one package all the way out the door.\n\n**Monday.** Counsel forwards the signed ESI protocol: static TIFF with a .DAT load file, seven metadata fields, plus flowsheet data native. Scope is one admission, 03/12–03/21, plus the ED encounter 60 days prior. You pull the source inventory: Epic inpatient chart, PACS imaging, Sunquest lab, the transcription archive, and one scanned outside-records packet.\n\n**Tuesday.** Export runs. Raw output is 4,911 pages. Processing removes 340 exact duplicate pages of the same faxed consent and flags three notes with multiple versions. You keep all three versions of each, labeled.\n\n**Wednesday.** Review. Counsel marks 22 pages for third-party PHI redaction and pulls 14 pages of risk-management material as privileged, withheld and listed on the privilege log — not silently dropped.\n\n**Thursday.** Redact, apply, flatten. Search the output for two redacted surnames: zero hits. Image, then Bates-stamp **MERCY000001–MERCY004238**. Build the .DAT with the seven agreed fields. Slip-sheet at MERCY004239 pointing to the native CSV.\n\n**Friday.** Encrypt, upload to the secure portal, capture the download confirmation. Log all eight fields. Cover letter states scope, sources, Bates range, 22 redactions, 14 pages withheld.\n\nEighteen months later you are asked what you sent. You open one row.",
